development.question_text:
This floor plan is U-shaped.
Two lengths are not marked.
Calculate the floor area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(10,0)--(10,6)--(7,6)--(7,2)--(3,2)--(3,6)--(0,6)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(10,2);
\node[below] at (5,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (10,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (1.5,6) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (8.5,6) {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A path of constant width $2$ m is built around the outside of a rectangular pool.
Calculate the area of the path (the shaded region).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.5]
\fill[blue!15] (0,0) rectangle (14,10);
\fill[white] (2,2) rectangle (12,8);
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (14,10);
\draw[thick] (2,2) rectangle (12,8);
\node[below] at (7,0) {$14\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,5) {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (0,9)--(2,9) node[midway,above] {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A swimming pool is shaped like a rectangle with a triangle on one end.
Calculate the surface area of the water.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(8,0)--(11,2.5)--(8,5)--(0,5)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (8,0)--(8,5);
\node[below] at (4,0) {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,2.5) {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (8,-0.6)--(11,-0.6) node[midway,below] {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A sports field is a trapezium with parallel sides $30$ m and $20$ m and a width of $12$ m. Turf costs $\$8$ per square metre.
Calculate the total cost of turfing the field.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.16]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(30,0)--(25,12)--(5,12)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (5,0)--(5,12);
\draw[dashed] (25,0)--(25,12);
\node[below] at (15,0) {$30\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (15,12) {$20\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (5,6) {$12\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A semicircle is cut from one long side of this rectangular metal tabletop.
Calculate the remaining area, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\fill[blue!15] (0,0) rectangle (10,6);
\fill[white] (2,6) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=3];
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (10,6);
\draw[thick] (2,6) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=3];
\node[below] at (5,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangular wall has a door and a window that will not be painted.
Calculate the area of wall to be painted.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\fill[blue!15] (0,0) rectangle (6,3);
\fill[white] (1,0) rectangle (2,2);
\fill[white] (3.5,1) rectangle (5,2);
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (6,3);
\draw[thick] (1,0) rectangle (2,2);
\draw[thick] (3.5,1) rectangle (5,2);
\node[below] at (3,0) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[below,font=\small] at (1.5,0) {$1\text{ m}$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (2,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[above,font=\small] at (4.25,2) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (5,1.5) {$1\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This tabletop is a rectangle with a triangle on each end.
Calculate its area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.5]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(10,0)--(13,3)--(10,6)--(0,6)--(-3,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(0,6);
\draw[dashed] (10,0)--(10,6);
\node[below] at (5,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (10,-0.7)--(13,-0.7) node[midway,below] {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
This garden bed is to be covered with mulch.
Each bag of mulch covers $7\text{ m}^{2}$, and bags cannot be split.
How many bags are needed?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.45]
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(12,0)--(12,6)--(6,10)--(0,6)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,6)--(12,6);
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (12,3) {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (6.4,6)--(6.4,10) node[midway,right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangular sheet of metal $12$ cm by $8$ cm has a smaller rectangle, $4$ cm by $x$ cm, cut out of it.
The area of metal that is left is $80\text{ cm}^{2}$.
Find the value of $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\fill[blue!15] (0,0) rectangle (12,8);
\fill[white] (7,2) rectangle (11,6);
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (12,8);
\draw[thick] (7,2) rectangle (11,6);
\node[below] at (6,0) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,4) {$8\text{ cm}$};
\node[below] at (9,2) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[right] at (11,4) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangular pool $15$ m long and $9$ m wide is surrounded by a paved path of constant width $1.5$ m. Paving costs $\$40$ per square metre.
Calculate the total cost of paving the path.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.32]
\fill[blue!15] (0,0) rectangle (18,12);
\fill[white] (1.5,1.5) rectangle (16.5,10.5);
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (18,12);
\draw[thick] (1.5,1.5) rectangle (16.5,10.5);
\node at (9,6) {$15\text{ m}\times 9\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (0,11)--(1.5,11) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
